# A `<=` bound on a three-clause loop must keep the CHECKED accessor, and this
# fixture proves it at runtime rather than by reading the emitted C: the last
# iteration indexes a[len(a)], so a correctly-checked program dies with
# `tycho: index 4 out of bounds (len 4)`. If for3_elidable_arr (src/tychoc.c:8380-8434) ever
# accepted `<=`, the loop would emit `(h_a).data[h_i]`, read one past the end and
# exit 0 -- and tests/run.sh's abort lane fails on "runtime abort did not fire".
# That is the whole reason this lives in tests/abort/ and not next to
# tests/bounds_noelide.ty: a wrong elision has to REDDEN something.
fn main():
    a := []int
    for i := 0; i < 4; i += 1:
        push(a, i)
    s := 0
    for i := 0; i <= len(a); i += 1:
        s = s + a[i]
    println(str(s))
